From f666306d819864dda7ce36aa4df55dbf75ef5edc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:59:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Compose the Windows node's wallet hold channel and lease
 readiness (installed control baseline)

The reviewed Windows lineage (ad4a72a refresher, 2afa673 keeper, 829a881 serving-first, e7e5057 fixes) starts from the
installed control snapshot lease-readiness-20261022 (commit 32fecf5 in the adapter-admission-review candidate). This tree's
Windows files were that snapshot minus the D1 wallet hold channel and the lease-readiness evidence; nothing in them is
absent from the snapshot. Taken verbatim from 32fecf5:

- windows/node/host.mjs      e41122d7 -> 9634cb40 (walletChannelStart/heartbeat/grant/revoke/hold ACK; leaseReadiness;
                                                  appZoneAdmitted; walletHeld routes refused)
- windows/node/agent.mjs     c2fe0fff -> 76cac355 (walletAdmission to enrollment, appZone admitted/closeDeployment wiring,
                                                  /v1/host/state leaseReadiness)
- windows/node/appzone.mjs   ba9d9bb1 -> 65cbb69a (admitted() re-check at splice time, closeDeployment)
- tests (new): windows-node-wallet-network-hold, windows-node-appzone-wallet-hold, windows-node-wallet-enroll,
  windows-node-lease-readiness

Composed, not copied:
- windows/node/network-enroll.mjs 2d97a0e1 -> bdc6019c: this tree's file plus ONLY the snapshot's walletAdmission block
  (kept last in the section, as in the snapshot). The snapshot's hostServices (host-service transport) and
  challengeReplica preservation are NOT composed: their runtime is not in this tree.

The channel stays opt-in (ENCLAVE_NETWORK_WALLET_HOLD=1 with an absolute ENCLAVE_NETWORK_AGENT_DIR); without it, or
without an agent that confirms the hold, an UNKNOWN wallet policy retires the domain exactly as before.
